lines=['# Actual 1 GB CPX02, no-swap Docker qualification','', 'Both pinned stacks passed correctness/restart/read-replay soak on the **same physical 1 GB / one-vCPU CPX02** (kernel RAM 977,784,832 bytes), sequentially, with an external CCX43 client. **This is not an unconditional cold-performance pass: the first Python writer-heavy run suffered severe memory pressure and its replay command exceeded 240 seconds without an observed OOM kill.** That entire pair was excluded, a replacement alternating pair was run with a disclosed 900-second command ceiling, and the table covers three completed pairs. No swap or larger fallback VM was used.','', '## Whole-stack footprint and performance','', 'Three alternating repetitions; table entries are medians of per-run values. Memory is the maximum sampled sum of the active stack’s exact container cgroups during that workload, then median across repetitions. RSS is reported separately in the machine-readable summary and double-counts shared pages.','', '| Stack | Workload | cgroup MiB | Successful RPC/s | p50 ms | p95 ms | p99 ms | RPC/s range |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|']
