lines +=['','## Correctness, persistence and lifecycle','', '- 22 records per stack: **21 deterministic records equal exactly**, plus one concurrency record equal by membership/multiplicity. Raw concurrent order was preserved and differed; it is not an ordering contract.', '- Both stacks passed canonical startup reads, full app/engine stop and restart, retained exact state and identical-key/payload replay. All six performance repetitions also verified the complete retained workload after restart.', '- Reader responses stay fixed at 16 × 64-byte messages. Single-actor writes: 1,000 requests; 32-actor writes: 2,000; reader and replay: 10,000 each. Eight concurrent client workers; fresh actors per repetition; no warmup in this tiny-host run.', '- Each stack passed at least 300 seconds of measured read/replay soak RPC execution, with zero errors. Writes are bounded and their full retained state is verified; this is not a multi-hour unbounded-ingestion test.', '- Exact container IDs, image/resource/network configurations, original Docker wait children and terminal exit-code readbacks are retained. Apps stop before the native engine. No unknown processes or containers were killed.', '- Host MemAvailable, host/cgroup memory pressure, CPU accounting, cgroup memory/events and swap were sampled at 250 ms. Initial runs had no extra RAM cap; the host and parent cgroup forbid swap.','', '## Lower aggregate budgets (not absolute minima)','', '| Stack | tiny.slice allowance MiB | Passed complete bounded gate | cgroup OOM kills | Lowest host MemAvailable MiB |','|---|---:|---|---:|---:|']
